{%- comment -%}
  TWX Safety Badges — Horizon theme block.

  Renders a product's safety features as compact pills. Designed for the product
  CARD (collection grids), but works anywhere `closest.product` resolves.

  Reads the same metafields the PDP spec block uses (see twx-product-specs.liquid);
  they are populated by the backfill app (backfill-app/src/index.js SPEC_KEYS):

    custom.toe_safety                  value IS the label   ("Steel Toe")
    custom.additional_safety_features  value IS the label, pipe-delimited
    global.waterproof                  flag -> "Waterproof"
    global.xrd_met_guard               flag -> "Met Guard"
    global.comfort_technology          value IS the label, pipe-delimited (off by default)

  DEFENSIVE VALUE HANDLING — the exact strings the CSV export writes are not yet
  confirmed, so this block tolerates both shapes without knowing which is used:

    * Flag fields render their fixed label for any affirmative-looking value
      ("Yes", "TRUE", "Waterproof", ...) and render NOTHING for anything in the
      negative list below. This is the important one: if `global.waterproof`
      turns out to carry "No" for non-waterproof product, those products must
      not get a "Waterproof" badge.
    * Value fields render the value verbatim, minus any negative entries, so a
      "Soft Toe" / "Non-Safety" product shows no toe badge.

  Once the real values are confirmed, tighten negative_values below.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign product_resource = closest.product
  assign mf = product_resource.metafields

  assign max_badges = block_settings.max_badges | default: 3

  comment
    Values that mean "this product does NOT have the feature". Compared
    case-insensitively against the whole trimmed value, pipe-wrapped on both
    sides so partial words can never match (e.g. "no" must not match "nomex").
  endcomment
  assign negative_values = '|no|none|n/a|na|false|0|null|not applicable|standard|soft|soft toe|non-safety|non safety|nonsafety|non-safety toe|no met guard|not waterproof|'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Pass 1 — collect candidate labels into a "~"-delimited string.
  Flag fields resolve to a fixed label; value fields contribute their own text.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture candidates -%}
  {%- if block_settings.show_toe_safety -%}
    {%- assign toe_values = mf.custom.toe_safety.value | split: '|' -%}
    {%- for toe_value in toe_values -%}
      {%- assign clean = toe_value | strip -%}
      {%- assign probe = '|' | append: clean | downcase | append: '|' -%}
      {%- unless clean == blank or negative_values contains probe -%}{{ clean }}~{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block_settings.show_waterproof -%}
    {%- assign wp = mf.global.waterproof.value | strip -%}
    {%- assign probe = '|' | append: wp | downcase | append: '|' -%}
    {%- unless wp == blank or negative_values contains probe -%}Waterproof~{%- endunless -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block_settings.show_met_guard -%}
    {%- assign mg = mf.global.xrd_met_guard.value | strip -%}
    {%- assign probe = '|' | append: mg | downcase | append: '|' -%}
    {%- unless mg == blank or negative_values contains probe -%}Met Guard~{%- endunless -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block_settings.show_additional -%}
    {%- assign extra_values = mf.custom.additional_safety_features.value | split: '|' -%}
    {%- for extra_value in extra_values -%}
      {%- assign clean = extra_value | strip -%}
      {%- assign probe = '|' | append: clean | downcase | append: '|' -%}
      {%- unless clean == blank or negative_values contains probe -%}{{ clean }}~{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block_settings.show_comfort -%}
    {%- assign comfort_values = mf.global.comfort_technology.value | split: '|' -%}
    {%- for comfort_value in comfort_values -%}
      {%- assign clean = comfort_value | strip -%}
      {%- assign probe = '|' | append: clean | downcase | append: '|' -%}
      {%- unless clean == blank or negative_values contains probe -%}{{ clean }}~{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Pass 2 — shorten for card display, then dedupe (a feature can appear in both
  toe_safety and the additional list) and count, so the overflow chip is
  accurate before anything renders.

  Shortening rule for parenthetical values:
    "Slip resistant (SR)"                        -> "SR"
    "Slip resistant (SRO)"                       -> "SRO"
    "BarnShield™ (livestock chemical resistant)" -> "BarnShield™"
  A SHORT parenthetical is the recognised industry abbreviation and says more
  than the words before it; a LONG one is a gloss, so the lead text wins. The
  full original value stays in the title attribute either way.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign candidate_list = candidates | split: '~'
  assign seen = '|'
  assign unique_labels = ''

  for candidate in candidate_list
    assign clean = candidate | strip
    if clean == blank
      continue
    endif

    assign display = clean
    if clean contains '('
      assign lead = clean | split: '(' | first | strip
      assign inner = clean | split: '(' | last | split: ')' | first | strip
      assign inner_size = inner | size
      if inner_size > 0 and inner_size <= 5
        assign display = inner
      elsif lead != blank
        assign display = lead
      endif
    endif

    comment
      Shoppers filter on "is it a safety toe", not on which material. Collapsing
      "Nano composite toe" / "Steel toe" / "Alloy toe" to one label also means
      the dedupe below leaves a single toe pill per product. Non-safety values
      ("Soft toe", "Non-safety toe") never reach here — negative_values drops
      them in pass 1, so this can't mislabel a soft-toe boot.
    endcomment
    assign display_probe = display | downcase
    if display_probe contains 'toe'
      assign display = 'Safety toe'
    elsif display_probe contains 'met guard'
      comment
        Same reasoning for met guards: "XRD® Met Guard" and "Met Guard" are the
        same feature to a shopper, and a product carrying both values would
        otherwise show two near-identical pills. One label, deduped below.
      endcomment
      assign display = 'Met guard'
    endif

    assign probe = '|' | append: display | downcase | append: '|'
    unless seen contains probe
      assign seen = seen | append: display | downcase | append: '|'
      comment
        Carry the original alongside the display label, "display^original", so
        the tooltip can still show the unabbreviated value.
      endcomment
      assign unique_labels = unique_labels | append: display | append: '^' | append: clean | append: '~'
    endunless
  endfor

  assign badges = unique_labels | split: '~'
  assign badge_count = badges | size

  comment
    Show every feature by default. When the merchant opts into a cap, a "+1"
    chip costs the same room as the badge it hides, so only collapse when at
    least two features would be hidden.
  endcomment
  assign display_limit = badge_count
  assign overflow = 0

  if block_settings.limit_badges
    assign potential_overflow = badge_count | minus: max_badges
    if potential_overflow > 1
      assign display_limit = max_badges
      assign overflow = potential_overflow
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if badge_count > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="twx-safety spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <ul class="twx-safety__list">
      {%- for badge in badges limit: display_limit -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign badge_label = badge | split: '^' | first
          assign badge_full = badge | split: '^' | last
          assign match = badge_full | downcase

          comment
            Colour by feature family, matched against the ORIGINAL value so the
            abbreviated labels ("SR") still classify correctly.
          endcomment
          assign tone = 'neutral'
          if match contains 'slip'
            assign tone = 'slip'
          elsif match contains 'toe'
            assign tone = 'toe'
          elsif match contains 'waterproof'
            assign tone = 'water'
          elsif match contains 'heat' or match contains 'thermal'
            assign tone = 'heat'
          elsif match contains 'eh protection' or match contains 'electrical'
            assign tone = 'electrical'
          elsif match contains 'met guard'
            assign tone = 'guard'
          elsif match contains 'barnshield'
            assign tone = 'brand'
          elsif match contains 'chemical' or match contains 'oil' or match contains 'viperguard'
            assign tone = 'shield'
          endif
        -%}
        <li
          class="twx-safety__badge twx-safety__badge--{{ tone }}"
          title="{{ badge_full | escape }}"
        >
          {{- badge_label | escape -}}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if overflow > 0 -%}
        <li class="twx-safety__badge twx-safety__badge--more">+{{ overflow }}</li>
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .twx-safety__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--padding-2xs, 0.25rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.15em 0.5em;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;

    /* Never truncate: a safety spec that reads "HEAT RESISTA…" is worse than
       one that takes two lines. Long labels wrap inside the pill and the pill
       is bounded by the card, so nothing overflows and nothing is cut off. */
    max-width: 100%;
    white-space: normal;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  /* Feature families — solid fills with white text throughout, so the pills
     read as one system.

     The grey and amber fills were LIGHT in an earlier revision (dark text on
     them); they are darkened here so white stays legible on every pill rather
     than leaving two odd ones out. Contrast against white, all >= 4.5:1 (WCAG
     AA) except the orange — see the note on --toe. */
  .twx-safety__badge {
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* #ff8200 against white is 2.5:1, below the 4.5:1 AA threshold — this is the
     one pill where white text is a legibility compromise rather than a win.
     Two ways out if it reads poorly in situ: dark text on this exact orange
     (8.4:1), or keep white and darken the fill to about #a85300 (5.4:1). */
  .twx-safety__badge--toe {
    background: #ff8200;
    border-color: #ff8200;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--slip {
    background: #5f5f5f;
    border-color: #5f5f5f;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--heat {
    background: #941114;
    border-color: #941114;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--water {
    background: #242f46;
    border-color: #242f46;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--brand {
    background: #5c4127;
    border-color: #5c4127;
  }

  /* Electrical hazard is yellow by convention, and yellow is the one hue white
     text cannot sit on: #f5c400 against white is 1.9:1, effectively unreadable,
     against near-black it is 11:1. This pill keeps dark text on purpose — the
     alternative that preserves white text is a dark amber (#8a6a00), which no
     longer reads as the EH yellow. */
  .twx-safety__badge--electrical {
    background: #f5c400;
    border-color: #f5c400;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--guard {
    background: #4a2c6b;
    border-color: #4a2c6b;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--shield {
    background: #4f5b6b;
    border-color: #4f5b6b;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--neutral {
    background: #4a4a4a;
    border-color: #4a4a4a;
  }

  .twx-safety__badge--more {
    background: none;
    border-color: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.25);
    border-style: dashed;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / var(--opacity-subdued-text, 0.7));
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "TWX Safety Badges",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows safety and comfort features as pills, read from the product's spec metafields. Renders nothing when a product has none of them set."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Features to show"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_toe_safety",
      "label": "Toe safety",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_waterproof",
      "label": "Waterproof",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_met_guard",
      "label": "Met guard",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_additional",
      "label": "Additional safety features",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_comfort",
      "label": "Comfort technology",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off by default — comfort tech is usually too long for a product card."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "limit_badges",
      "label": "Limit how many badges show",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off shows every feature a product has."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_badges",
      "label": "Maximum badges",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
      "info": "Extra features collapse into a \"+N\" chip.",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.limit_badges }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "Left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "Right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "TWX Safety Badges",
      "category": "Product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
